7
00:00:16,780 --> 00:00:19,260
[iQIYI]

8
00:00:20,300 --> 00:00:22,940
[Present]

9
00:00:23,220 --> 00:00:26,100
♫Where’s that love people are saying?♫

10
00:00:26,100 --> 00:00:29,500
♫To always be by each other’s sides♫

11
00:00:29,500 --> 00:00:32,580
♫The love that’s willing to sacrifice everything♫

12
00:00:32,580 --> 00:00:35,580
♫Everything even my own life♫

13
00:00:35,580 --> 00:00:39,060
♫Do they really exist? I’d rather not believe it♫

14
00:00:39,060 --> 00:00:42,140
♫I don’t think I’ll ever fall for anyone♫

15
00:00:42,140 --> 00:00:45,380
♫Love? I don’t find it interesting♫

16
00:00:45,380 --> 00:00:48,460
♫Sorry about that♫

17
00:00:48,940 --> 00:00:51,500
♫But then who are you?♫

18
00:00:51,500 --> 00:00:55,500
♫To make my heart keep fluttering♫

19
00:00:55,500 --> 00:00:57,900
♫Please tell me♫

20
00:00:58,140 --> 00:01:01,220
♫What’s happening with my heart?♫

21
00:01:01,220 --> 00:01:04,580
♫It can’t be, why am I feeling this?♫

22
00:01:04,580 --> 00:01:07,660
♫Oh, my heart is pounding so fast♫

23
00:01:07,660 --> 00:01:10,740
♫Time freezes whenever I see you♫

24
00:01:10,740 --> 00:01:14,100
♫I wonder why every time you smile♫

25
00:01:14,100 --> 00:01:17,380
♫Something in your eyes make me go weak♫

26
00:01:17,380 --> 00:01:20,580
♫Oh no, this is real–it’s not a dream♫

27
00:01:20,580 --> 00:01:23,460
♫Or is the love that people are saying...♫

28
00:01:23,460 --> 00:01:25,340
♫Is it you?♫

29
00:01:30,220 --> 00:01:32,060
♫Is it you?♫

30
00:01:32,060 --> 00:01:34,050
[Flaming Chains of Love]

31
00:01:35,600 --> 00:01:38,330
[Previously]
If you find a pink shell, you’ll get to make one wish.

32
00:01:38,600 --> 00:01:39,620
There it is!

33
00:01:39,950 --> 00:01:42,350
[Thunder]
May everyone be happy!

34
00:01:42,370 --> 00:01:45,870
[Bua]: A bad storm is coming. You’d better stay here tonight, Young Master.

35
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:48,070
Does that mean we won’t be able to go back until tomorrow?

36
00:01:48,370 --> 00:01:49,930
[Fai]: Will there be any storm today?

37
00:01:50,130 --> 00:01:50,930
[Bua]: No, Miss.

38
00:01:51,070 --> 00:01:53,570
Then, go tell Uncle Boonsong this.

39
00:01:53,620 --> 00:01:55,700
Don’t tell me you want to go back right now.

40
00:01:55,780 --> 00:01:56,729
Nope.

41
00:01:59,300 --> 00:02:02,180
[Panee]: I already warned you not to cause Fai any trouble.

42
00:02:02,200 --> 00:02:03,900
What do you want me to do then?

43
00:02:05,330 --> 00:02:06,950
[Akanee]: Fai is here to help the Little One.

44
00:02:07,270 --> 00:02:08,199
There’s nothing to worry about now.

45
00:02:08,330 --> 00:02:09,580
[Fai]: Are you going to leave me here?

46
00:02:09,600 --> 00:02:11,280
[Kaphrao]: Then, get up. Get up!

47
00:02:16,670 --> 00:02:18,150
How old are you this year?

48
00:02:20,770 --> 00:02:21,570
22.

49
00:02:24,570 --> 00:02:28,850
You’re an adult now, a grown-ass woman.

50
00:02:32,700 --> 00:02:34,850
You’re not a kid anymore.

51
00:02:36,329 --> 00:02:38,380
You don’t need to do everything my aunt says.

52
00:02:38,930 --> 00:02:41,350
If you don’t want to do it, just say it out loud.

53
00:02:41,900 --> 00:02:43,980
so that you won’t trouble yourself later.

54
00:02:53,530 --> 00:02:55,870
As if Miss Panee would let me say no to her.

55
00:02:57,400 --> 00:03:00,080
Are you trying to get me scolded even more?

56
00:03:00,800 --> 00:03:04,020
Just do as I say. Leave the rest to me.

57
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:06,530
How can I trust you?

58
00:03:09,730 --> 00:03:12,380
Whatever, it’s your choice.

59
00:03:17,730 --> 00:03:18,670
I’m leaving.

60
00:03:21,270 --> 00:03:26,880
Me too, but…let me drop you off.

61
00:03:39,400 --> 00:03:40,480
Whatever.

62
00:04:13,070 --> 00:04:15,730
Why are you following me? Just go home.

63
00:04:16,570 --> 00:04:20,079
I need to make sure you won’t sneak out to suck up to my dad.

64
00:04:20,529 --> 00:04:21,680
Urgh!!!

65
00:04:33,970 --> 00:04:34,770
Phrao!

66
00:04:35,530 --> 00:04:36,330
Nod!

67
00:04:56,330 --> 00:04:57,620
How did you get here?

68
00:04:57,870 --> 00:04:59,480
I’m here to surprise you.

69
00:04:59,480 --> 00:05:03,020
- Aww, you’re as sweet as ever.
- Right?

70
00:05:03,370 --> 00:05:05,320
Hey, you’re too skinny.

71
00:05:05,330 --> 00:05:06,700
Waiting for your treat.

72
00:05:07,070 --> 00:05:08,450
Sure! Just name the date.

73
00:05:08,580 --> 00:05:09,880
Okay.

74
00:05:14,070 --> 00:05:16,780
Aww, miss you so much!

75
00:05:18,070 --> 00:05:20,350
I remember you told me you live here.

76
00:05:20,600 --> 00:05:22,970
I’ve moved to Surat now.

77
00:05:23,270 --> 00:05:25,680
We can meet more often from now on.

78
00:05:26,600 --> 00:05:28,300
Why did you move here?

79
00:05:28,930 --> 00:05:35,250
My relative is opening a hotel here, and also plans to open a restaurant; so I’m here to help.

80
00:05:35,330 --> 00:05:36,620
That sounds great.

81
00:05:37,050 --> 00:05:39,480
Well, what a coincidence.

82
00:05:41,550 --> 00:05:44,770
I think it’s more like destiny.

83
00:05:50,300 --> 00:05:53,180
If you’re done catching up, hurry and get back to work.

84
00:05:54,330 --> 00:05:57,270
What work? It’s off the clock now.

85
00:05:57,900 --> 00:06:01,120
It’s overtime work, to make up for what I helped you earlier.

86
00:06:01,650 --> 00:06:02,530
What?

87
00:06:02,800 --> 00:06:05,580
I couldn’t get any work done because I was helping you with the lawn mowing.

88
00:06:05,770 --> 00:06:07,130
Got loads of them piling up over my head.

89
00:06:07,400 --> 00:06:09,650
- But I’ll go to work tomorrow any–
- Phrao.

90
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:11,450
Just get on with your work.

91
00:06:11,700 --> 00:06:13,450
I’ll come see you again.

92
00:06:14,170 --> 00:06:15,920
We have plenty of time to meet up after this.

93
00:06:19,330 --> 00:06:20,650
Don’t you think so?

94
00:06:31,500 --> 00:06:33,120
I’ll go wait at the office.

95
00:06:41,200 --> 00:06:42,000
It’s okay.

96
00:06:57,970 --> 00:06:59,770
So, what work is it?

97
00:07:01,400 --> 00:07:02,900
I want to talk to you about the resort.

98
00:07:03,730 --> 00:07:04,530
Yeah?

99
00:07:04,930 --> 00:07:10,850
We’ll create ecotourism there starting with a homestay at the locals’ houses including Lom’s cabin too, right?

100
00:07:11,270 --> 00:07:13,900
That’s right. We’ve already talked about this.

101
00:07:16,130 --> 00:07:17,850
Well, I’ll start drafting the plan then.

102
00:07:19,530 --> 00:07:20,500
Is that all?

103
00:07:21,770 --> 00:07:24,250
What about the second project? When should we start?

104
00:07:25,400 --> 00:07:28,850
Look, do we really need to talk about this now?

105
00:07:29,150 --> 00:07:31,350
We haven’t even started the first one yet.

106
00:07:32,570 --> 00:07:34,120
So that we’ll have more time to prepare.

107
00:07:36,300 --> 00:07:39,220
Why? Are you mad because I interrupted your precious time with your friend?

108
00:07:39,300 --> 00:07:40,950
You’re damn right! So what?

109
00:07:42,330 --> 00:07:44,520
Why can’t she just find a damn job in Bangkok?

110
00:07:47,930 --> 00:07:50,050
Hey! Where do you think you’re going?

111
00:07:50,070 --> 00:07:50,670
Home!

112
00:07:50,670 --> 00:07:54,020
You dragged me here just to say that? Hey!

113
00:07:56,670 --> 00:07:58,500
That’s it? Why now?

114
00:08:24,600 --> 00:08:30,950
It’s more like destiny. Destiny…Destiny…Destiny.

115
00:08:31,730 --> 00:08:33,450
Obviously not just a friend.

116
00:09:05,770 --> 00:09:07,150
This one is good.

117
00:09:07,150 --> 00:09:09,420
Thank you.

118
00:09:23,770 --> 00:09:28,980
Nod, can I have it?

119
00:09:30,530 --> 00:09:31,330
Only this once.

120
00:09:42,800 --> 00:09:43,600
Thank you!

121
00:09:53,300 --> 00:09:55,650
Phrao! Where are you, Phrao?

122
00:09:56,370 --> 00:09:58,130
Over here, Nod.

123
00:10:08,300 --> 00:10:09,600
Thanks a lot, Nod.

124
00:10:14,470 --> 00:10:18,370
No problem. I’ll wait outside then.

125
00:10:18,730 --> 00:10:20,950
You’re the sweetest!

126
00:12:32,600 --> 00:12:34,450
Nod! What are you doing here?

127
00:12:34,530 --> 00:12:37,070
I bought you sticky rice and grilled pork skewers–your favourite.

128
00:12:38,070 --> 00:12:40,380
Wow, thank you!

129
00:12:41,870 --> 00:12:45,780
I’m out looking for seafood ingredients for my relative’s restaurant.

130
00:12:45,780 --> 00:12:49,180
Oh, you’ve come to the right place. I’ll take you to the fisherman’s wharf.

131
00:12:49,200 --> 00:12:52,650
Let’s take my car then. You can be my navigator.

132
00:12:52,770 --> 00:12:53,570
Sure!

133
00:12:53,930 --> 00:12:54,730
Let’s go.

134
00:13:04,930 --> 00:13:06,170
Can I eat them in your car?

135
00:13:06,370 --> 00:13:09,320
Of course. They’re really good.

136
00:13:09,370 --> 00:13:10,170
I’m not sharing then.

137
00:13:23,170 --> 00:13:24,320
Who’s that?

138
00:13:32,130 --> 00:13:36,380
Can you please remove those too, so it won’t look so messy?

139
00:13:36,380 --> 00:13:36,780
Bua.

140
00:13:37,600 --> 00:13:38,480
Where’s Kaphrao?

141
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:42,680
Oh, she went to the fisherman’s wharf with her friend.

142
00:13:44,400 --> 00:13:45,200
Friend?

143
00:13:45,500 --> 00:13:47,980
Yes, her friend came early in the morning.

144
00:13:48,100 --> 00:13:49,870
I think she said she’s looking for seafood ingredients.

145
00:13:50,870 --> 00:13:53,150
Which friend? What’s her name? What does she look like?

146
00:13:54,730 --> 00:13:58,120
I think she’s called Nod. If I’m not wrong, I mean.

147
00:13:59,080 --> 00:14:03,450
As for her appearance, she looks so pretty and neat, Young Master.

148
00:14:03,450 --> 00:14:05,120
They’re taking really good care of each other.

149
00:14:05,120 --> 00:14:09,520
She even brought Miss Phrao breakfast. Miss Phrao also seems to be very fond of her.

150
00:14:15,470 --> 00:14:19,070
So, should I go get Miss Phrao for you?

151
00:14:20,070 --> 00:14:21,600
No need. It’s not like I care.

152
00:14:23,670 --> 00:14:26,780
That bloody loafer, came here every f***ing day!

153
00:14:48,730 --> 00:14:54,800
Here, I’ll show you how they’re sorting them out. You can be sure all seafood is fresh here.

154
00:14:55,070 --> 00:14:55,770
That’s lots of them!

155
00:14:55,770 --> 00:15:02,320
This is the first station. They’re sorting out small fish and baitfish.

156
00:15:02,500 --> 00:15:06,000
This station is for medium-size fish. We have plenty for you to choose from.

157
00:15:06,500 --> 00:15:09,620
They’re all fresh from the sea. Look there.

158
00:15:23,020 --> 00:15:24,950
It’s nothing. Let’s go.

159
00:15:28,150 --> 00:15:30,480
This station is for big fish.

160
00:15:30,530 --> 00:15:31,720
- So big!
- Right?

161
00:15:31,720 --> 00:15:35,580
Have you ever seen this one? We have various types of fish here.

162
00:15:43,070 --> 00:15:43,870
Nod!

163
00:15:44,670 --> 00:15:46,070
Here you go.

164
00:15:46,700 --> 00:15:47,500
Wow.

165
00:15:50,370 --> 00:15:55,530
I’ll give it to my relative and see what we can do with it.

166
00:15:55,730 --> 00:16:00,220
Thanks. I’ll also help talk to Uncle Ak for any possible discount.

167
00:16:01,700 --> 00:16:05,200
Do you usually take care of the work here at the fisherman’s wharf?

168
00:16:06,500 --> 00:16:11,950
Not really, I’m actually Fai’s assistant. I just do whatever I’m assigned to.

169
00:16:12,500 --> 00:16:16,220
Uncle wants me to try out everything before deciding which work I like the most.

170
00:16:17,330 --> 00:16:19,880
Why is he so nice to you?

171
00:16:20,150 --> 00:16:25,050
If I hadn’t known, I would’ve thought you were one of his daughters who owns this place.

172
00:16:25,600 --> 00:16:30,420
Geez, don’t say that. Fai already hates me to her guts these days.

173
00:16:33,070 --> 00:16:35,470
Anyway, do you have anything else to do today?

174
00:16:36,100 --> 00:16:37,670
I’m working half-day today.

175
00:16:38,770 --> 00:16:40,120
Let’s go find something to eat then.

176
00:16:40,120 --> 00:16:41,220
Sure.

177
00:16:41,900 --> 00:16:42,980
[Nod]: Should we go now?
[Phrao]: Mhm.

178
00:16:44,070 --> 00:16:45,700
[Phrao]: I need to grab my bag first.

179
00:16:45,930 --> 00:16:46,730
[Nod]: Sure.

180
00:16:47,570 --> 00:16:50,320
[Nod]: What do you want to eat? I’m starving.

181
00:16:55,500 --> 00:16:56,870
[Phrao]: Look, tumblers.

182
00:16:58,530 --> 00:16:59,880
The colours look so sweet.

183
00:16:59,900 --> 00:17:00,950
Yeah, very sweet.

184
00:17:02,170 --> 00:17:02,970
Oh, this one!

185
00:17:05,300 --> 00:17:07,579
Yeah, or this one.

186
00:17:08,569 --> 00:17:11,880
[Phrao]: It’s so cute. Baby pink.

187
00:17:14,730 --> 00:17:15,420
Should we get them?

188
00:17:15,650 --> 00:17:16,849
[Nod]: Yes, but I’ll pay.

189
00:17:16,849 --> 00:17:19,220
[Phrao]: Aww, thank you, Sugar Mummy.

190
00:17:19,670 --> 00:17:20,849
[Nod]: No problem, babe.

191
00:17:21,130 --> 00:17:22,770
[Phrao]: Maybe, I should get one of these bags.

192
00:17:23,130 --> 00:17:25,079
[Nod]: They’re pretty.
[Phrao]: And big too.

193
00:17:25,079 --> 00:17:26,550
[Phrao]: Look.
[Nod]: Huh?

194
00:17:27,000 --> 00:17:29,280
[Phrao]: Isn’t it cute?
[Nod]: Yeah, so cute.

195
00:17:29,280 --> 00:17:31,450
Right? Wow…

196
00:17:33,620 --> 00:17:34,580
[Phrao]: Hey, this one’s cute!

197
00:17:36,780 --> 00:17:37,720
[Phrao]: So cold.

198
00:17:39,780 --> 00:17:41,350
[Phrao]: Freezing?
[Nod]:It’s so good!

199
00:17:41,350 --> 00:17:42,920
Let me try it too.

200
00:17:47,700 --> 00:17:48,850
[Nod]: How is it?
[Phrao]: Awesome!

201
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:49,800
How’s the drink?

202
00:17:49,970 --> 00:17:50,770
[Phrao]: Try it.

203
00:17:51,400 --> 00:17:52,120
[Phrao]: Like it?

204
00:17:52,120 --> 00:17:55,820
[Phrao]: This one is good too.

205
00:17:59,770 --> 00:18:01,450
Looking so bloody happy, huh?

206
00:18:16,930 --> 00:18:17,730
Fai!

207
00:18:19,730 --> 00:18:23,300
Oh, look who’s here. What a coincidence.

208
00:18:23,970 --> 00:18:27,800
What are you doing here? Don’t tell me you’re stalking me.

209
00:18:28,200 --> 00:18:30,050
What? Who’s stalking?

210
00:18:30,050 --> 00:18:35,150
I’m here to get some toys for the mine worker's kid, and just came across this air hockey here.

211
00:18:36,330 --> 00:18:38,380
When I was a kid, no one could beat me at it.

212
00:18:39,500 --> 00:18:41,300
Should we play a round then?

213
00:20:09,270 --> 00:20:10,330
One more?

214
00:20:10,870 --> 00:20:14,870
That’s enough. I’m hungry. I still need to go back to do the laundry.

215
00:20:15,900 --> 00:20:20,450
That’s great. I’m hungry too. It’s my treat this time.

216
00:20:23,970 --> 00:20:26,120
[Phrao]: What should we order?
- [Nod]: They all look tasty.

217
00:20:34,270 --> 00:20:37,350
Look, they have squids too. You like them, don’t you?

218
00:20:38,600 --> 00:20:40,270
Let’s order Squid Tom Yum then.

219
00:20:40,970 --> 00:20:42,050
You remember?

220
00:20:42,870 --> 00:20:44,570
One squid Tom Yum, please.

221
00:20:45,900 --> 00:20:48,980
I remember everything about you.

222
00:20:49,770 --> 00:20:53,750
But I don’t remember a thing. I can’t remember what you like to eat.

223
00:20:55,070 --> 00:21:02,780
I like Kaphrao (holy basil). I’ll have one stir-fried crispy pork with holy basil, please.

224
00:21:05,170 --> 00:21:08,100
What about you, Miss Fai?

225
00:21:13,200 --> 00:21:14,670
ike Kaphrao too.

226
00:21:20,300 --> 00:21:24,850
I’ll have stir-fried crispy pork in extra size with lots of holy basil leaves, please.

227
00:21:33,070 --> 00:21:34,870
Since when have you liked holy basil?

228
00:21:37,570 --> 00:21:39,180
I’ve always liked it.

229
00:21:42,200 --> 00:21:43,000
Really?

230
00:21:44,770 --> 00:21:52,850
So, we’ll have one pot of rice, stir-fried crispy pork with lots of holy basil in extra size, and squid Tom Yum.

231
00:21:53,380 --> 00:21:54,050
That’s all, right?

232
00:21:54,850 --> 00:21:55,920
That’d be all.

233
00:22:03,730 --> 00:22:04,750
I’m starving.

234
00:22:07,700 --> 00:22:09,850
You seem to know her well, Nod.

235
00:22:11,130 --> 00:22:16,550
Of course, I do. We used to eat and sleep together for many years.

236
00:22:16,730 --> 00:22:20,680
What about you? How long have you known her?

237
00:22:23,670 --> 00:22:29,320
Well, since she was seven–long before she moved to Bangkok and met you there.

238
00:22:32,170 --> 00:22:35,550
So, I guess you must know about her Phi Jah (Big Sis).

239
00:22:35,550 --> 00:22:36,530
Nod!

240
00:22:41,770 --> 00:22:42,570
Why?

241
00:22:45,370 --> 00:22:46,720
Who’s Phi Jah?

242
00:22:50,130 --> 00:22:52,120
It’s the person she likes.

243
00:22:54,600 --> 00:22:58,180
That’s weird. She’s never told you about that?

244
00:22:58,180 --> 00:22:59,620
Nod, stop it.

245
00:22:59,800 --> 00:23:01,250
Are you two really close?

246
00:23:05,100 --> 00:23:08,980
Nod, it was just a joke–why did you bring it up? I wasn’t being serious.

247
00:23:09,750 --> 00:23:12,220
It’s nothing. We were just joking around.

248
00:23:17,370 --> 00:23:21,020
The food is so slow. I’ll go to the loo first.

249
00:23:54,000 --> 00:23:55,730
She took you out and ditched you there.

250
00:23:56,300 --> 00:23:58,320
What would you do if I wasn’t around to drop you home?

251
00:23:58,470 --> 00:24:01,570
Something urgent came up for her. Wasn’t it you who offered to drop me home in the first place?

252
00:24:01,730 --> 00:24:03,170
Hold on. Got something to ask you.

253
00:24:04,470 --> 00:24:06,400
What now? Can it wait until tomorrow?

254
00:24:07,700 --> 00:24:08,900
But I want to know it now.

255
00:24:10,270 --> 00:24:11,070
So selfish.

256
00:24:11,600 --> 00:24:12,400
Hey, wait!

257
00:24:15,700 --> 00:24:16,930
Who the hell is Jah?

258
00:24:18,330 --> 00:24:19,130
What?

259
00:24:20,970 --> 00:24:23,880
Is she someone you’re seeing? Someone you like? Or your first girlfriend?

260
00:24:23,880 --> 00:24:25,720
And how long have you known her?

261
00:24:27,370 --> 00:24:28,800
Why on earth would you want to know?

262
00:24:30,370 --> 00:24:35,080
Because I want to. Does my dad know about this?

263
00:24:37,400 --> 00:24:39,180
None of your business. Move!

264
00:24:39,180 --> 00:24:42,350
Hey! Can’t you just tell me? Hey!

265
00:24:44,070 --> 00:24:47,980
Come any closer and I’ll call the police to arrest you for trespassing.

266
00:24:47,980 --> 00:24:48,720
Go away!

267
00:24:50,800 --> 00:24:52,300
Geez, I was just asking.

268
00:24:53,200 --> 00:24:54,480
And I’m not telling you!

269
00:24:55,900 --> 00:24:58,250
What’s so secret? Would it kill you to say it?

270
00:25:01,120 --> 00:25:02,450
Who the hell?

271
00:25:19,450 --> 00:25:21,720
[Phone ringing]

272
00:25:26,500 --> 00:25:27,730
What, Boss Rose?

273
00:25:29,600 --> 00:25:31,450
Why do you sound so grumpy?

274
00:25:31,930 --> 00:25:34,400
I just want to place an order for seafood.

275
00:25:34,970 --> 00:25:37,720
Din and I are going to have a seafood party for our workers.

276
00:25:38,170 --> 00:25:40,880
We’d like you to send us some shrimps and crabs.

277
00:25:40,900 --> 00:25:43,670
Okay, I’ll have someone take care of it by tomorrow morning.

278
00:25:44,370 --> 00:25:45,200
Is that all?

279
00:25:47,000 --> 00:25:49,880
Come on, don’t hang up on me so fast.

280
00:25:50,550 --> 00:25:54,880
Did you have a fight with Miss Phrao? Is that why you’re so grumpy?

281
00:25:59,270 --> 00:26:01,350
What? Who says I love that silly Gremlin?

282
00:26:03,020 --> 00:26:08,250
Besides, her friend just slipped out today that she already has someone she likes.

283
00:26:11,470 --> 00:26:13,650
I see, someone is being heartbroken.

284
00:26:17,100 --> 00:26:19,050
I told you I don’t like her!

285
00:26:21,300 --> 00:26:24,300
All right, I heard that. You don’t have to be so pissed.

286
00:26:24,800 --> 00:26:30,850
Listen Fai, you should try to be nice to her. Don’t just keep picking on her, or else she’ll hate you.

287
00:26:31,670 --> 00:26:34,000
So what? Who cares?

288
00:26:37,370 --> 00:26:42,050
That’s too bad. I was actually going to give you some advice on how to pursue a girl–

289
00:26:42,130 --> 00:26:44,200
to make Miss Phrao like you.

290
00:26:50,450 --> 00:26:52,670
What should I do then?

291
00:26:55,670 --> 00:26:57,420
I thought you said you don’t like her.

292
00:26:58,420 --> 00:27:02,880
Well, just for interest’s sake.

293
00:27:06,000 --> 00:27:08,080
If you like her

294
00:27:09,220 --> 00:27:11,080
and want her to love you,

295
00:27:11,320 --> 00:27:14,450
you must try to please her and be nice to her.

296
00:27:15,350 --> 00:27:18,980
Take her out to wonderful places and to eat something delicious.

297
00:27:18,980 --> 00:27:20,750
She’ll definitely fall for you.

298
00:27:25,700 --> 00:27:27,680
So, any other details?

299
00:27:29,470 --> 00:27:32,220
Let me suggest my “3As” technique.

300
00:27:32,570 --> 00:27:36,420
The one that’s perfect for you is “A for (being) attentive”.

301
00:27:38,770 --> 00:27:44,520
You need to find out what she likes and try to pamper her with those things.

302
00:27:44,520 --> 00:27:49,580
Quit picking on her, and only do whatever she pleases. Got it?

303
00:27:55,400 --> 00:27:57,450
You two already went to the island.

304
00:27:58,200 --> 00:27:59,870
Have you come up with any ideas to pitch me?

305
00:28:00,070 --> 00:28:04,550
We both agree that this project should be divided into two phases.

306
00:28:04,550 --> 00:28:08,680
For the first phase, we’ll start by providing a simple homestay service.

307
00:28:08,680 --> 00:28:11,620
So that local villagers could take part in it.

308
00:28:11,620 --> 00:28:15,050
It’ll also help generate more income for them.

309
00:28:16,070 --> 00:28:19,950
We can use Miss Lom and Miss Blew’s cabin as our selling point.

310
00:28:19,950 --> 00:28:23,380
And back it up with the Princess’s story when she used to stay there.

311
00:28:23,750 --> 00:28:25,580
That’s a brilliant idea.

312
00:28:26,000 --> 00:28:31,180
But will it affect the villagers’ way of living? Have you thought about that too?

313
00:28:31,280 --> 00:28:36,220
Yes, that’s why we’d like to start with only a few cabins first. Then, we’ll see the response.

314
00:28:36,220 --> 00:28:41,920
After that, we can adjust the plan along the way so it won’t affect the calm and peaceful life of local people there.

315
00:28:44,470 --> 00:28:49,250
And to make it more interesting, I think we should also have a diving activity.

316
00:28:49,400 --> 00:28:51,850
I’m sure it’ll help attract more tourists to come to the island.

317
00:28:54,200 --> 00:28:56,170
What a perfect combination.

318
00:28:56,420 --> 00:28:59,570
One is to look after the cozy accommodation.

319
00:28:59,970 --> 00:29:01,930
The other is to take care of tourist activities.

320
00:29:03,170 --> 00:29:04,880
I approve of this project.

321
00:29:09,130 --> 00:29:14,180
Now, you two should write a full business plan and show it to me after this.

322
00:29:15,020 --> 00:29:16,250
Give me your best shot.

323
00:29:42,170 --> 00:29:49,350
[Rose]: If you like her and want her to love you, you must try to please her and be nice to her.

324
00:29:49,350 --> 00:29:53,580
Take her out to wonderful places and to eat something delicious.

325
00:29:53,580 --> 00:29:55,650
She’ll definitely fall for you.

326
00:29:57,600 --> 00:29:59,200
Anything on what I told you to find out?

327
00:30:00,500 --> 00:30:07,600
Listen, Young Master. I didn’t just ask around but I also used my nosy skill to pry out more information.

328
00:30:08,170 --> 00:30:12,680
I sneaked into Miss Phrao’s room and took a quick look at her purse.

329
00:30:12,680 --> 00:30:15,020
I found a picture of her and her dad when she was a kid.

330
00:30:15,470 --> 00:30:21,050
It was taken at the dam. If I’m not mistaken, I think it also has a water park there.

331
00:30:22,480 --> 00:30:23,780
A water park?

332
00:30:23,780 --> 00:30:29,020
Yes, I remember Miss Phrao once told me she wanted to go there.

333
00:30:31,130 --> 00:30:33,150
Still love playing like a kid as I thought.

334
00:30:33,370 --> 00:30:36,980
Come on, Young Master. Anyone would want to act like a kid once in a while.

335
00:30:36,980 --> 00:30:40,450
Unlike someone who’s always working her butt off.

336
00:30:43,600 --> 00:30:48,480
All right then, thanks a lot. And don’t tell her I asked you about this.

337
00:30:48,500 --> 00:30:53,120
Geez, Young Master. You can trust me. I won’t say anything–my lips are sealed.

338
00:30:53,550 --> 00:30:55,520
- Enjoy your food then.
- Yes.

339
00:31:02,500 --> 00:31:04,200
I want you to go to the dam with me.

340
00:31:06,000 --> 00:31:06,800
The dam?

341
00:31:07,770 --> 00:31:08,570
Mhm.

342
00:31:10,100 --> 00:31:12,870
Just want to check it out in case we might get some ideas for our project.

343
00:31:18,900 --> 00:31:21,000
But if you don’t want to, I can go alone.

344
00:31:22,000 --> 00:31:23,120
Of course, I’ll go!

345
00:31:23,120 --> 00:31:27,180
I want to go there. When I was a kid, my dad used to take me there.

346
00:31:28,330 --> 00:31:29,450
You want to go?

347
00:31:29,450 --> 00:31:30,420
Mhm.

348
00:31:30,700 --> 00:31:31,880
Then, I’m not going.

349
00:31:33,200 --> 00:31:34,520
What the hell is wrong with you?

350
00:31:36,200 --> 00:31:37,500
Beg me first.

351
00:31:40,870 --> 00:31:43,350
Then, I’m not going. So annoying!

352
00:31:43,800 --> 00:31:45,820
Hey, wait! Hold on!

353
00:31:45,820 --> 00:31:48,950
Let’s go then. I was only kidding back there.

354
00:31:52,300 --> 00:31:53,920
Then, beg me first.

355
00:31:56,600 --> 00:31:59,450
Come with me, please. Pleaseee.

356
00:32:00,770 --> 00:32:01,570
Mhm.

357
00:32:03,130 --> 00:32:05,070
And make sure you wear something pretty.

358
00:32:05,330 --> 00:32:07,470
Otherwise, people might think I’m there with a servant.

359
00:32:12,470 --> 00:32:13,720
Foul mouth!

360
00:32:15,650 --> 00:32:17,480
But since you’re cute,

361
00:32:17,750 --> 00:32:19,050
I’ll forgive you.

362
00:33:27,080 --> 00:33:29,820
What are you up to, my pretty lady?

363
00:33:29,930 --> 00:33:32,120
Come give me a hug.

364
00:33:35,300 --> 00:33:37,920
Are you going out somewhere, dear?

365
00:33:38,370 --> 00:33:39,850
Do you need me for anything, Auntie?

366
00:33:41,200 --> 00:33:44,550
My friend and her daughter will come to our house today.

367
00:33:44,730 --> 00:33:47,300
I want you to take her daughter out and show her around.

368
00:33:51,470 --> 00:33:53,350
Does it have to be today?

369
00:33:54,050 --> 00:33:57,920
Yes, isn’t it your day off today?

370
00:33:59,680 --> 00:34:01,680
Or do you have other plans?

371
00:34:05,970 --> 00:34:08,449
Well, I…

372
00:34:10,770 --> 00:34:14,170
Please do me a favour and show her around. Just do it for me.

373
00:34:18,900 --> 00:34:20,520
Could it be some other days?

374
00:34:21,469 --> 00:34:23,679
I already promised it to Jinda, dear.

375
00:34:23,679 --> 00:34:29,219
If you don’t do it, my friend might see me as someone who kept going back on my words.

376
00:34:29,370 --> 00:34:30,730
Do it for me. Please.

377
00:34:37,730 --> 00:34:38,530
Okay.

378
00:34:39,900 --> 00:34:40,699
My good girl.

379
00:34:42,770 --> 00:34:45,750
I’ll make some desserts for you.

380
00:35:03,130 --> 00:35:06,650
Miss Phrao, you look so pretty!

381
00:35:07,000 --> 00:35:09,730
Wow, can you turn around?

382
00:35:11,570 --> 00:35:16,680
Wow, I almost couldn’t recognise you! So pretty indeed.

383
00:35:16,680 --> 00:35:21,180
Trust me, if Young Master sees you in this dress, her jaw will definitely drop.

384
00:35:21,270 --> 00:35:22,300
No way.

385
00:35:26,700 --> 00:35:27,530
I’m going then.

386
00:35:27,800 --> 00:35:30,550
Okay, bye! Good luck!

387
00:35:39,600 --> 00:35:41,120
You’re here early.

388
00:35:47,930 --> 00:35:53,670
I’m afraid I can’t go with you today. I need to do something for my aunt–it’s urgent.

389
00:36:00,530 --> 00:36:02,500
Can we go next week instead?

390
00:36:07,870 --> 00:36:09,620
Well, that’s all right.

391
00:36:14,930 --> 00:36:19,280
How about I’ll tell Uncle Yod to take you there in the afternoon instead?

392
00:36:23,750 --> 00:36:24,780
Mhm.

393
00:36:40,580 --> 00:36:42,780
Oh, thank you.

394
00:36:46,270 --> 00:36:47,070
Thank you.

395
00:36:57,770 --> 00:37:01,850
So, are you usually always this busy?

396
00:37:02,970 --> 00:37:04,180
Why do you ask?

397
00:37:04,800 --> 00:37:10,180
Well, you’ve been staring at your phone since we arrived here.

398
00:37:13,870 --> 00:37:14,670
Yes.

399
00:37:15,800 --> 00:37:16,820
You’re busy?

400
00:37:16,820 --> 00:37:18,120
You’re nosy!

401
00:37:20,470 --> 00:37:24,980
Well, I’ve ordered Chicken Nanban for you.

402
00:37:25,320 --> 00:37:27,980
I don’t know if you’ll like it.

403
00:37:27,980 --> 00:37:30,980
Oh, here they are!

404
00:37:31,770 --> 00:37:33,520
Thank you.

405
00:37:33,520 --> 00:37:37,220
Wow, it looks so tasty. Thank you. That one is for you.

406
00:37:37,750 --> 00:37:41,620
You ordered them, so eat them yourself. Hurry up so we can go home.

407
00:37:46,100 --> 00:37:50,550
Do you have to do something after this? Why are you in a rush?

408
00:37:54,570 --> 00:37:56,220
Yes, I have to go somewhere.

409
00:37:56,600 --> 00:37:58,950
Where is it? Can I go with you?

410
00:38:00,370 --> 00:38:02,050
Just mind your own business.

411
00:38:03,130 --> 00:38:05,270
I only agree to take you here because my aunt said so.

412
00:38:05,470 --> 00:38:07,480
Stop asking so many questions–it’s annoying.

413
00:38:12,870 --> 00:38:16,750
And quit using that stupid voice. Why would you do that? It sounds so awkward.

414
00:38:16,750 --> 00:38:19,950
If you think it’s cute, I’m telling you it’s giving me a creep.

415
00:38:23,420 --> 00:38:25,130
Wait, where are you going?

416
00:38:25,470 --> 00:38:26,270
Toilet.

417
00:38:43,350 --> 00:38:45,730
So pretty, look. See this?

418
00:38:45,920 --> 00:38:50,330
Aww, don’t tell me you already ordered it.

419
00:38:50,580 --> 00:38:52,220
But of course, I did.

420
00:38:57,500 --> 00:38:58,300
Oh.

421
00:38:59,950 --> 00:39:02,880
Jee, what’s wrong, dear?

422
00:39:04,000 --> 00:39:05,930
Fai just ditched me, Mum.

423
00:39:07,770 --> 00:39:09,520
She completely ignored me.

424
00:39:09,770 --> 00:39:11,350
She took me out to eat but…

425
00:39:12,870 --> 00:39:16,380
she barely said a word to me. She just ate and left.

426
00:39:17,370 --> 00:39:18,880
Where did she go then?

427
00:39:18,900 --> 00:39:24,080
I don’t know! She said something urgent  came up, then she just left me there alone.

428
00:39:27,130 --> 00:39:28,320
Something urgent?

429
00:39:39,380 --> 00:39:41,670
Why are you dropping me off here, Uncle Yod?

430
00:39:41,930 --> 00:39:46,500
Well, Young Master told me to drop you off here. She’s probably waiting inside.

431
00:39:48,300 --> 00:39:49,950
I see.

432
00:39:49,950 --> 00:39:51,920
- Thank you.
- No problem.

433
00:40:22,900 --> 00:40:24,750
I thought you said you were busy.

434
00:40:26,570 --> 00:40:27,370
You’re here?

435
00:40:32,100 --> 00:40:36,880
It’s for you. These too.

436
00:40:45,070 --> 00:40:46,650
Eat, so we can get going.

437
00:40:50,170 --> 00:40:52,000
I finished earlier than expected.

438
00:40:55,470 --> 00:40:59,320
My aunt made me go on a date this morning.

439
00:41:05,200 --> 00:41:07,930
Really? How was it?

440
00:41:10,930 --> 00:41:12,930
Nothing much. It was pretty annoying.

441
00:41:21,570 --> 00:41:24,670
Don’t you feel anything when I go out with someone else?

442
00:41:26,530 --> 00:41:27,930
What should I feel then?

443
00:41:35,930 --> 00:41:37,270
Don’t you want to ask me anything?

444
00:41:39,500 --> 00:41:40,700
What should I ask then?

445
00:41:47,370 --> 00:41:48,750
You, nitwit.

446
00:41:51,000 --> 00:41:51,900
Time to go now.

447
00:41:54,730 --> 00:41:57,550
Huh? Is she mad again?

448
00:42:28,750 --> 00:42:31,680
- Here.
- Thanks.

449
00:42:39,930 --> 00:42:41,550
Do you come here often?

450
00:42:42,870 --> 00:42:43,670
No.

451
00:42:44,170 --> 00:42:46,170
You seem to know your way around here though.

452
00:42:47,870 --> 00:42:50,270
Have you ever heard of an internet? Try using it.

453
00:42:57,470 --> 00:42:58,270
This is good.

454
00:43:02,200 --> 00:43:03,000
Try it.

455
00:43:07,800 --> 00:43:08,600
Have a bite.

456
00:43:37,330 --> 00:43:40,330
Wouldn’t you be in trouble if Miss Panee knows you’re here with me?

457
00:43:42,730 --> 00:43:46,300
She doesn’t know. I told Uncle Yod to pick you up, remember?

458
00:43:47,170 --> 00:43:48,550
What about when we go back?

459
00:43:50,400 --> 00:43:51,800
You can walk home then.

460
00:44:00,670 --> 00:44:02,330
You seem different lately.

461
00:44:13,400 --> 00:44:14,200
How?

462
00:44:15,930 --> 00:44:18,170
You’ve never been this nice to me.

463
00:44:18,600 --> 00:44:20,450
All you did was keep picking a fight.

464
00:44:29,470 --> 00:44:30,270
That’s because I…

465
00:44:35,070 --> 00:44:35,870
I…

466
00:44:39,700 --> 00:44:40,500
I…

467
00:44:43,400 --> 00:44:44,200
I…

468
00:44:49,200 --> 00:44:51,020
I want to go on that slide.

469
00:44:54,330 --> 00:44:55,130
Let’s go then.

470
00:44:55,900 --> 00:44:56,700
What?

471
00:44:56,800 --> 00:44:58,200
Come on. Get moving.

472
00:44:58,700 --> 00:45:00,000
I haven’t put on a life jacket yet.

473
00:45:00,070 --> 00:45:01,380
Go put it on over there.

474
00:45:01,470 --> 00:45:02,920
Do we have to do it now?

475
00:45:02,920 --> 00:45:03,770
Or we won’t get to do it.

476
00:45:03,770 --> 00:45:06,120
- It’ll be too crowded.
- No one’s going to play it.

477
00:45:06,120 --> 00:45:07,480
There’s so many people over there.

478
00:45:21,020 --> 00:45:23,680
♫Where’s that love people are saying?♫

479
00:45:23,680 --> 00:45:26,920
♫To always be by each other’s sides♫

480
00:45:26,920 --> 00:45:30,080
♫The love that’s willing to sacrifice everything♫

481
00:45:30,080 --> 00:45:33,220
♫Everything even my own life♫

482
00:45:33,220 --> 00:45:36,520
♫Do they really exist? I’d rather not believe it♫

483
00:45:36,520 --> 00:45:39,750
♫I don’t think I’ll ever fall for anyone♫

484
00:45:39,750 --> 00:45:42,850
♫Love? I don’t find it interesting♫

485
00:45:42,850 --> 00:45:46,150
♫Sorry about that♫

486
00:45:46,620 --> 00:45:49,150
♫But then who are you?♫

487
00:45:49,150 --> 00:45:53,080
♫To make my heart keep fluttering♫

488
00:45:53,080 --> 00:45:55,720
♫Please tell me♫

489
00:45:55,720 --> 00:45:58,780
♫What’s happening with my heart?♫

490
00:45:58,780 --> 00:46:02,150
♫It can’t be, why am I feeling this?♫

491
00:46:02,150 --> 00:46:05,280
♫Oh, my heart is pounding so fast♫

492
00:46:05,280 --> 00:46:08,450
♫Time freezes whenever I see you♫

493
00:46:08,450 --> 00:46:11,680
♫I wonder why every time you smile♫

494
00:46:11,680 --> 00:46:14,850
♫Something in your eyes make me go weak♫

495
00:46:14,850 --> 00:46:18,120
♫Oh no, this is real–it’s not a dream♫

496
00:46:18,120 --> 00:46:21,180
♫Or is the love that people are saying...♫

497
00:46:21,330 --> 00:46:22,720
♫Is it you?♫

498
00:46:27,770 --> 00:46:29,220
The weather is so nice.

499
00:46:34,330 --> 00:46:36,200
You seem to like it here a lot.

500
00:46:37,670 --> 00:46:41,320
I do. I miss those times when I came here with my dad.

501
00:46:50,070 --> 00:46:53,130
I’m sure your dad already knows you come back here today.

502
00:46:57,700 --> 00:46:59,950
This place has changed so much.

503
00:47:01,970 --> 00:47:03,870
I wonder what he’s like now.

504
00:47:06,870 --> 00:47:08,800
He’s probably having a good time up there.

505
00:47:17,600 --> 00:47:19,970
Your dad might have run into my mum by now.

506
00:47:21,300 --> 00:47:22,850
They’ve probably become friends.

507
00:47:26,570 --> 00:47:30,820
I’ll ask Dad to tell your mum that you like to pick on me.

508
00:47:34,300 --> 00:47:40,180
Surely, Mum will know I got falsely accused by a silly Gremlin.

509
00:47:55,200 --> 00:47:57,780
Don’t you remember anything about your mum?

510
00:48:06,000 --> 00:48:08,420
I only saw her in the picture.

511
00:48:10,800 --> 00:48:14,080
But I could feel that she loved me so much.

512
00:48:18,470 --> 00:48:22,680
You might be stubborn, hot-headed, and a bit of a bully.

513
00:48:24,380 --> 00:48:26,820
But I’m sure your mum loved you a lot.

514
00:48:28,450 --> 00:48:30,780
Just like Uncle Ak, he also loves you a lot.

515
00:48:34,400 --> 00:48:35,970
Don’t rub it on my face.

516
00:48:37,400 --> 00:48:40,120
You stole my dad’s love from me.

517
00:48:41,170 --> 00:48:44,720
I’m serious. Uncle loves you so much.

518
00:48:46,870 --> 00:48:50,720
I don’t know what’s going on between you and your father.

519
00:48:51,330 --> 00:48:54,370
But I can feel that you both really love each other.

520
00:48:56,870 --> 00:49:02,920
I want you to put your bias aside, and open up to him while you still can.

521
00:49:05,000 --> 00:49:08,750
Don’t be like me and wait until he’s gone.

522
00:49:12,470 --> 00:49:17,380
As someone who no longer has a dad and a mum, that’s all I could say.

523
00:49:47,600 --> 00:49:48,400
Hey.

524
00:49:51,170 --> 00:49:51,550
What?

525
00:49:51,550 --> 00:49:53,150
Can you take a picture for me?

526
00:49:55,670 --> 00:49:58,420
Right here, it’s so pretty.

527
00:50:02,100 --> 00:50:02,900
Sure.

528
00:50:07,530 --> 00:50:08,570
Make sure I look tall.

529
00:50:11,770 --> 00:50:15,880
1 2 3. Again, 1 2 3.

530
00:50:18,600 --> 00:50:19,870
I’m so good at this.

531
00:50:20,530 --> 00:50:22,180
It’s because the model is pretty.

532
00:50:24,470 --> 00:50:26,450
Okay, not so bad.

533
00:50:27,100 --> 00:50:29,650
Here, do it for me too.

534
00:50:31,700 --> 00:50:34,200
Take it. You’re not the only one who wants a picture here.

535
00:50:38,400 --> 00:50:39,750
Make it look nice.

536
00:50:39,930 --> 00:50:40,730
Sure.

537
00:50:43,720 --> 00:50:48,680
1 2 3. Here, take a look.

538
00:50:48,680 --> 00:50:49,850
Let me see.

539
00:50:51,400 --> 00:50:55,520
Hmm, you’re better than I thought.

540
00:50:59,970 --> 00:51:01,580
Let’s take a picture together.

541
00:51:07,200 --> 00:51:08,000
Why?

542
00:51:10,930 --> 00:51:16,780
As a reminder…that we once came here together.

543
00:51:21,700 --> 00:51:22,500
Come on.

544
00:51:29,500 --> 00:51:30,300
Ready?

545
00:51:37,200 --> 00:51:38,730
- Wow.
- Is it good?

546
00:51:39,520 --> 00:51:40,370
So pretty.

547
00:51:47,200 --> 00:51:49,080
Wow, look at the view there.

548
00:51:55,270 --> 00:51:57,420
But I look prettier. Look.

549
00:52:42,800 --> 00:52:45,270
Thank you for taking me out today.

550
00:52:48,330 --> 00:52:50,880
If you’re feeling grateful, you should do it properly.

551
00:52:52,000 --> 00:52:56,550
You need to list out all the things I’ve done for you. So that you won’t forget them.

552
00:52:57,120 --> 00:52:59,870
Did you do it because you expected something in return?

553
00:53:00,870 --> 00:53:02,900
Or just to hold it over my head later?

554
00:53:05,170 --> 00:53:07,250
You always think badly of me.

555
00:53:08,330 --> 00:53:10,450
I just want you to see…

556
00:53:11,020 --> 00:53:12,720
that I can be nice too.

557
00:53:13,770 --> 00:53:15,600
I don’t think badly of you.

558
00:53:21,930 --> 00:53:22,930
Then, smile a bit.

559
00:53:25,200 --> 00:53:26,000
What for?

560
00:53:28,070 --> 00:53:31,820
Please. To end the day happily.

561
00:53:33,270 --> 00:53:34,250
Smile like this.

562
00:53:52,900 --> 00:53:53,700
Happy now?

563
00:53:55,330 --> 00:53:56,130
I’m going in.

564
00:54:35,870 --> 00:54:37,250
Are you here to see Kaphrao?

565
00:54:38,200 --> 00:54:42,280
I’m here to see you. Can we talk?

566
00:54:43,730 --> 00:54:44,530
I’m busy.

567
00:54:46,170 --> 00:54:47,780
It’s about Kaphrao.

568
00:54:48,250 --> 00:54:49,920
It won’t be long.

569
00:54:56,470 --> 00:54:57,530
Go on then.

570
00:55:01,800 --> 00:55:08,720
Kaphrao and I have known each other for so long–since when we were in school.

571
00:55:10,020 --> 00:55:14,420
You know how I feel about her, don’t you?

572
00:55:16,670 --> 00:55:17,750
So what?

573
00:55:19,400 --> 00:55:26,880
I came back this time because I intend to never let her go again.

574
00:55:30,200 --> 00:55:31,650
Why are you telling me this?

575
00:55:31,970 --> 00:55:33,200
Go tell her then.

576
00:55:36,130 --> 00:55:43,750
I saw you with her but I really can’t tell what relationship it is that you have with her.

577
00:55:44,570 --> 00:55:46,720
Let me get this straight then.

578
00:55:48,800 --> 00:55:54,420
If you don’t have feelings for Kaphrao, can you please step aside?

579
00:55:55,700 --> 00:56:01,050
Don’t give her hope if you’re not serious about her.

580
00:56:40,570 --> 00:56:42,330
You’ve split up with Jee since afternoon.

581
00:56:42,770 --> 00:56:44,000
Why are you only home now?

582
00:56:47,130 --> 00:56:48,950
I went out somewhere else.

583
00:56:49,970 --> 00:56:52,330
With whom? What’s their name? Do I know them?

584
00:56:55,200 --> 00:56:58,320
I’m a grown-up now, Auntie. You don’t need to be so worried.

585
00:56:58,320 --> 00:56:59,880
I can take care of myself.

586
00:57:05,370 --> 00:57:12,250
That’s right. Now, I’m just a bother to you, aren’t I?

587
00:57:12,650 --> 00:57:14,120
You don’t listen to me anymore.

588
00:57:14,400 --> 00:57:21,550
Come on, Auntie. Please don’t be upset. It was really for work.

589
00:57:26,200 --> 00:57:29,680
I know that sometimes you find me annoying.

590
00:57:32,180 --> 00:57:36,220
But it’s all out of good intentions.

591
00:57:41,470 --> 00:57:47,620
I want you to be with someone you deserve, and only have the best things in life.

592
00:57:52,970 --> 00:57:53,930
I know.

593
00:58:00,470 --> 00:58:06,380
You know how much I love you, don’t you?

594
00:58:13,300 --> 00:58:18,730
If you love me, don’t ever let me down, okay?

595
00:58:24,100 --> 00:58:24,900
Yes.

596
00:58:27,300 --> 00:58:28,800
I’ll take that as a promise.

597
00:59:39,170 --> 00:59:46,550
[Nod]: I came back this time because I intend to never let Phrao go again.

598
00:59:47,600 --> 00:59:49,470
